text:
mia: Quick heads-up — onboarding a customer onto the new JS SDK in Cloudflare Workers and running into runtime errors. Auth token refresh fails, and `crypto` is undefined in a few of our sample apps.

sam: Same here. Repro in our sandbox: globalThis.crypto.subtle missing. Tried fast-webcrypto-shim — fixes crypto but bloats the bundle and breaks some devtools.

priya: Also seeing `AbortController is not defined` during streaming + retry flow. Workers has fetch but not some Node globals we assume in SDK builds.

alex: Minimal repro I used:

```
addEventListener('fetch', event => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  // auth refresh uses subtle.digest
  const h = crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', new TextEncoder().encode('x'))
  fetch('https://api.redwood.com/generate', {signal: controller.signal})
})
```

That errors with crypto undefined and then later AbortController missing in some runtimes.

priya: Workaround that helped us temporarily: don't bundle node polyfills, instead ship a tiny "edge shim" that checks for globals and falls back to lightweight implementations. e.g.

```
if (typeof globalThis.crypto === 'undefined') {
  globalThis.crypto = { subtle: { digest: async () => /* tiny impl */ } }
}
if (typeof AbortController === 'undefined') {
  globalThis.AbortController = class { constructor(){ this.signal = {} } }
}
```

But this is fragile and not great for customers.

mia: Proposal: SDK should publish an explicit "edge" ESM build target that:
- avoids Node APIs entirely
- uses feature-detection (no heavy ponyfills)
- provides opt-in tiny shims for only missing primitives (AbortController, minimal crypto.digest)
- documents behavior (what's polyfilled vs not)
- includes a sample app for CF Workers and Cloudflare Pages

sam: Agreed. Also note: auth refresh should avoid fs/child_process dependencies and prefer a direct fetch-to-token endpoint flow in the edge build so token rotation doesn't rely on node-only libs.

alex: I'll open a PR: add rollup/tsup target `esm-edge` that tree-shakes out node libs, add examples/workers-edge/sample.js and an e2e smoke test. tagging @priya for docs and TS definitions.

deploy-bot: ci: created pipeline run workers-edge-e2e #3456

priya: One more thing — TypeScript defs are referencing `NodeJS.Timeout` in retry types which breaks `tsc` for strict `lib: ['webworker']`. We should make types conditional (DOM/web) for the edge build.

mia: Action items: alex -> PR for edge build + sample app; priya -> docs + TS defs update; sam -> verify auth flow in dedicated customer repro; mia -> follow up on rollout plan and add an internal note in the onboarding checklist. Label this thread `edge-dx` and `devex`. :thumbsup:
